  "content_description": "Priorities Action Item",
  "content_text_body": "Because your top performers execute so well and can take on a lot of work, they may become overburdened with many high-priority areas, particularly in collaborative environments. The goal is to ensure your top performers are not being put at risk for burnout and attrition.\n\n### Assess top performers' priorities\n\nDetermine if your top performers' priorities are leading to burnout or attrition by asking yourself these questions.\n\n* Do your top performers take on too many high-priority areas? \n\n* Are your top performers involved in a lot of collaborative work? \n\n* Are your top performers doing work that does not require their unique skill set?\n\n* Are your top performers showing signs of burnout? \n\nRead this article on [Collaborative Overload](https://hbr.org/2016/01/collaborative-overload) for more information.\n\nRead this article: [How To Tell If Your Team Is Burnt Out And What To Do About It](http://www.forbes.com/sites/dailymuse/2013/06/04/how-to-tell-if-your-team-is-burnt-out-and-what-to-do-about-it)",
